perfcached (0.3.0~rc18-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An empty joiner pulls its own bootstrap from a ready peer and is
    ready when the stream ends (S83); the write-path push coalesces into
    one datagram per peer (S105, 289k -> 349k SET/s at depth 64).
  * libperfd 0.2.7: a failover probes before adopting, members marked
    down are re-dialled in the background, and the fleet's membership
    pushes are acted on (S104, S107).  Four defects found by the S107
    verification fixed, one of which left a push reaching only one
    worker's clients.
  * The RESP door speaks RedisJSON's JSON.* (S86); the JSON validator
    is strict about primitives.
  * Identity and term files are text, checked and refusing (S106); a
    copied identity is refused again (S108) and a held join is held out
    loud.

