perfcached (0.3.0~rc14-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libperfd 0.2.4: TCP keepalive on every link, and an idle ping that
    retires a standby that died while idle - marking its member down
    with the reason - so a failover never adopts a dead connection.
    Every link carries the time of its last accepted reply.
  * libperfd 0.2.3: a handle can say what it found - the daemon's
    version from the member list and each member's state from this
    handle's own dials; the members reply carries version and rev.
  * Ledger: S104 (failover onto dead standbys, with the operator's rule:
    hold every member, use any live one, fail only when none is), S105
    (the write-path coalescing buffer S73 decided on and never built),
    S106 (a text node identity file).

 -- Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 10:07:00 +1000

perfcached (0.3.0~rc13-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A peer's record count and start kind are written only by its own
    heartbeat.  The master's keepalive, a JOIN and an ASSIGN list know
    neither and used to store zeros, so every non-master's view of the
    master flapped once a second and the backfill sender election
    sometimes saw the lowest id as empty and self-designated: two
    senders for one backfill, in every CI run.
  * members reports, per member, this node's view of its record count
    and start kind - what the election reads.
  * stalebackfilltest probes that view and waits one heartbeat after
    a fill before judging it.

 -- Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 08:11:00 +1000

perfcached (0.3.0~rc12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Test-only over rc11.  eagertest's quiet window opens on the restarted
    node's own completion, from a line written after its restart, and
    covers every node's counter - the wait it had was satisfied by an
    older line and sampled a sender mid-cycle (rc10, rc11).
  * stalebackfilltest waits out the cold window before restarting a
    node, so only the lowest id is a sender, as the suite assumes.

 -- Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 23:05:00 +1000

perfcached (0.3.0~rc11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A stale backfill flag no longer fires when the ids reshuffle: a walk
    starts only while its target still reports itself cold, and a flag
    whose target is established is dropped.  This was rc10's red, and
    the false "backfilled node N after its restart" seen on the fleet.
  * A punched-out hugetlb group is secured before it is handed out again;
    an empty pool refuses the re-commit instead of faulting (SIGBUS).
  * The give-back no longer re-faults what it just released: a cold slot
    has no header until it is re-committed.
  * Give-back decides under the arena lock and punches without it, one
    madvise per run of groups; bounded per tick by [memory] shrink_step_mb.
  * The ceiling is a latched state (at_ceiling, at_ceiling_since) with a
    red card; the overview counts the fleet's members, not this node's
    peers.

 -- Yury Kirsanov <yury@kfi.net.au>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +1000

perfcached (0.3.0~rc10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A founding node keeps the id its identity proposes: become_master()
    asks the same allocator every joiner goes through instead of
    stamping itself node 1, so a whole-fleet restart no longer
    renumbers the fleet around whichever node booted first.
  * The status page reports what the WAL and RDB are doing rather than
    that they are "on"; the history graphs state the window they cover
    and are twice as tall, ruled at the quarters.

